cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Air Hockey Vision: A Multi-Threaded Real-Time Computer Vision Interface for High-Frequency Human-Computer Interaction"
abstract: >
  Air Hockey Vision is a Python software system that integrates real-time markerless
  hand tracking (Google MediaPipe) with a physical air hockey simulation. The system
  employs a multi-threaded architecture to decouple camera acquisition, landmark
  detection, and game rendering into independent execution threads, achieving stable
  60 Hz interactive performance. Signal noise is eliminated via an adaptive 2D One
  Euro Filter, and kinematic forward extrapolation compensates for end-to-end
  pipeline latency. The project serves as a reference implementation for low-latency
  HCI systems and as a pedagogical platform for teaching signal filtering, predictive
  kinematics, and elastic collision physics.
